{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
  "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A clearing futures commodity merchant, an FCM, such as Petitioner, has standing to sue contract markets and clearing organizations of contract markets under Section 25 (b)(1) of the act for their bad faith failure to enforce rules that are required by the act and by the Commodity Futures Trading Commission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The cause of action, we understand, requires that there be a showing of bad faith."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For purposes of this case, the Court may assume that the word \"transaction\" in Section 25(b)(1) is limited to the purchase and sale of futures and options contracts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the argument that if we accept your view of it, allowing the FCM to sue, then there could be multiple liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (Mr. Stewart)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean the clearing FCM assumes direct contractual liability to the clearinghouse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Where is the clear -- there\nis no clear definition. There is no definition\nwhatsoever, anywhere, of \"transaction.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Pincus)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINCUS: Well, certainly a floor trader\nis because that's someone who is trading for his own\naccount. A floor broker who's merely representing a\ncustomer is just like someone at a house closing, if you\ncan't make the house closing you appoint someone to\nclose the house. They aren't the ones who engage in the\ntransaction; you do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: I was under the impression\nfrom the briefs, and maybe I'm wrong, that you did not\ndefend the reasoning of the Second Circuit. Am I right\nor wrong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Pincus)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINCUS: No. Our position is, again,\nthe \"on or subject to\" language, we believe, quite\nclearly refers to trades and that Congress's technical\ncorrect substitution of registered entities doesn't\nchange that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Pincus)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PINCUS: The harm -- two categories of\nharm: First, a lack of clarity. We don't know, as I\nsaid, how far back are we going. The statute requires,\nfor customers that are not trade, not exchange members,\nthey have to go to an introducing broker. They have to\ngo then to an FCM."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Pincus, will you\nsatisfy me on one point. I -- I understand your\nargument about what \"transaction\" means. But even if I\naccept that argument, explain to me again why \"or\nsubject to the rules\" doesn't add anything?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Days",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1265",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c0e044580014a1113a75c9585c9aeda050551be17228a84b3ed53efc1748b8ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c0e044580014-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DAYS: Your Honors, Mr. Pincus has\nidentified what he views as some temporal gap between\nthe entering into a contract and the involvement of this\n-- the clearing FCM. That simply is not the case.\nKlein had a prior commitment to clear\nEisler's trade; so even at the time that Eisler was\ntrading, that had to be done with the understanding that\nKlein was going to back him up.\nIf one looks at the gray brief at page 21,\nit references to the rule of Knight -- rules of Knight\n116 and 118 that make this very clear. The story is, as\nwe've indicated, that throughout this process the\nclearing FCM is financially liable and, therefore, is on\nthe hook.\nWhen Congress enacted the statute, it was\nconcerned with protecting the public and maintaining\ncredibility. We think that this cause of action, this\nexpress cause of action for allowing FCMs to sue, is\nmost reliant to the objectives of Congress: The\nfaithful execution by an FCM that deals directly with\nthese entities, the clearinghouse and the commodity\ncontract market. Thank you very much."
    },
